<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8480" root="حفر" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَفِيرٌ</span></b>  is of the measure <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَعِيلٌ</span> in the sense of the
measure <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَفْعُولٌ</span> [meaning <i>Dug, excavated, hollowed out,</i> or <i>cleared out, in the ground</i>]. (TA.)
[Hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَكِيَّةٌ حَفِيرَةٌ</span> <i>A newly-dug well;</i> as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَفَرٌ</span></b> . (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also this last word. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also,
(IAar, S, A, K,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَفِيرَةٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَفْرٌ</span></b> , (A,) [or
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَفَرٌ</span></b> , q. v., and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُفْرَةٌ</span></b> , as is shown by an explanation of its pl. (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُفَرٌ</span>) in the Ham p. 562,]
<i>A grave.</i> (IAar, S, A, K.)

